https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VExw77xJsBQ  (Capo 0)

TIP:  This is another one of those songs where the verses are sharped after the first verse creating messy chords.  And in this case you start without a capo and then add it to the 1st fret (if you want to play along with the recording).  Otherwise just ignore the capo setting and repeat the chords (play what you see).

TIP:  George's singing style, with his vocal hesitations (which is what made George, George) is a little tricky.  I added commas where he pauses briefly but if they're distracting just sing the melody in your head and you'll do fine.
   

